4137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined-1small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined-1small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3828011083">February 9, 2021</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted"><strong>Didn’t quite hit the mark</strong><br /><br />I’m really sad that I didn’t love this one because I have become a fan of Courtney Dean. I was excited about this because it had all the makings of something I would enjoy but it just felt like it was lacking somewhere. The characters were all fine but it just felt like everything was rushed and nothing felt developed. I liked the premise and the glimpses I got of Amani and Alek were good, but it just wasn’t enough for me to really get into them. The same goes for the secondary characters as well. What was really everyone’s motivations? I understood the council and Anastasia a little but what was Aleksei getting out of this?? The ending was setting up Eva and Christoff’s story, but I felt no desire to care about them as they really didn’t do much in this book. <br /><br />Overall not a decent story but it needed to be fleshed out more. </span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action">